Hi again,

(sorry if this appears a bit offtopic here, but the time series
business is quite GIS related).

The strptime() functions is in the source code at:
./src/main/datetime.c

Some if tests are lacking else statements, so I am not surprised
that R also accepts a tz="GRASS" time zone :-) On the other hand
it may be impossible to implement all existing names. Tests seem
to be done only for "GMT" and "UTC", other names are taken literally.

Enough for today on this,
 Markus


